    a <ontology/EvidenceQuote/#resource> ;
    rdfs:label "Evidence for Vanilla used in Chocolate & Confectionery: P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Dictionary of Trade Products (1892), scan p. 409"@en ;
    <ontology/quoteText/#resource> "VANILLA: an exquisite perfume and aromatic, the thin pod-like capsule of the Vanilla planifolia, a native of South America. Vanilla is one of the most esteemed of all aromatics, and very expensive, costing five or six guineas the pound. It is used to flavour chocolate and confectioneries, and is much esteemed on the Continent as an ingredient in some stimula..."@en ;
    <ontology/retrievalMode/#resource> "direct_sentence" .
